Campus Events API verification — local Docker Compose — 2026-11-01 (Asia/Karachi)
Environment: baseUrl=http://localhost:8080

Automated frontend suite:
- npm run lint: PASS
- npm test: PASS (8 tests, 0 failed)
- npm run build: PASS

API checks via PowerShell HTTP requests (the Postman collection is exported separately):
- GET /api/events?page=0&size=12 without cookie: 200; page envelope keys content,page,size,totalElements,totalPages,first,last; size=12; totalElements=555; 12 rows.
- GET /api/auth/me without cookie: 401; GET /api/registrations without cookie: 401; POST /api/events without cookie: 401.
- GET /api/events/1: 200; GET /api/events/999999: 404.
- Student login: 200; response sets jwt_token with HttpOnly; /me: 200; logout: 200; /me after logout: 401.
- Valid-length bad login: 401, generic “Invalid email or password”. Duplicate signup: 409 “Email already registered”. Tampered cookie on /me: 401.
- Student POST /api/events: 403. Admin POST /api/events: 201; DB created_by=1 despite body createdBy=999999. Owner update: 200; different admin update: 403.
- Invalid category, lowercase category, capacity 0, and missing required fields: 400 each.
- Registration with fake userId: 201; DB row user_id=6 (cookie user), event_id=557. Duplicate: 409; capacity-one event full: 409; missing event: 404; null eventId: 400.
- Delete event with registration: 409; cancel own registration: 204; delete after cancellation: 204.
- Malformed JSON POST /api/events: 400.
- 201-character title: 500, generic “Unexpected server error.”, no SQL/JDBC/constraint text.
- 201-character location: 500, generic “Unexpected server error.”, no SQL/JDBC/constraint text.
- PUT /api/events/{id} with 201-character title: 500; with 201-character location: 500. Temporary update-test event then deleted (204).

Headless Postman-compatible collection run via Newman:
- 36 requests executed; 38 assertions; 36 passed, 2 failed as expected: title >200 chars and location >200 chars each returned 500 instead of expected 400.
- Full CLI output and JSON report are in this folder. `results.json` has session-cookie values redacted before keeping it as evidence.

Database SQL checks executed with `docker compose exec -T db mysql -ucampus -pcampus123 campus_events`:
SELECT COUNT(*) AS events FROM events; -- 555
SELECT COUNT(*) AS registrations FROM registrations; -- 1000
SELECT COUNT(*) AS users FROM users; -- 100
SELECT id,created_by,title FROM events WHERE id=557; -- 557, 1, QA DB ownership event
SELECT id,user_id,event_id FROM registrations WHERE id=1002; -- 1002, 6, 557
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM events WHERE id=557; -- 0 after cleanup
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM registrations WHERE id=1002; -- 0 after cleanup

Temporary event and registration were removed. After the Newman run, DB counts were again 555 events, 1000 registrations, and 100 users; no temporary event title remained.

Visual evidence was supplied by the user and is saved in `screenshots/events-list-evidence.png`, `screenshots/login-form-evidence.png`, and `screenshots/admin-dashboard-evidence.png`. Browser automation permission remained blocked, so I reviewed the supplied images rather than capturing them. They show desktop layouts; responsive checks at 1440/1280/680/mobile widths remain unverified.
